Host: Windows 11, QEMU emulator version 11.1.0 (v11.1.0-12130-ge470268ff4), TCG (no KVM).
Method: wall time from QEMU process start to the NOVA_BOOT_OK serial line,
qemu -M q35 -m 512M -serial stdio -display none; OVMF = build/edk2-code.fd
(copied from QEMU's share/edk2-x86_64-code.fd) as pflash. Limine's
'timeout: 3' countdown is inside every number. Runs were sequential;
host load was not controlled, so differences under ~1 s are noise.
Script (not committed, scratch helper):
  | """Wall time from QEMU start to NOVA_BOOT_OK on serial. Usage: boottime.py img fw runs"""
  | import subprocess, sys, time
  | 
  | QEMU = r"C:\Program Files\qemu\qemu-system-x86_64.exe"
  | img, fw, runs = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], int(sys.argv[3])
  | for i in range(runs):
  |     args = [QEMU, "-M", "q35", "-m", "512M", "-drive", f"file={img},format=raw",
  |             "-serial", "stdio", "-display", "none", "-no-reboot"]
  |     if fw != "seabios":
  |         args[1:1] = ["-drive", f"if=pflash,format=raw,readonly=on,file={fw}"]
  |     t0 = time.monotonic()
  |     p = subprocess.Popen(args, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
  |     got = None
  |     for line in p.stdout:
  |         if b"NOVA_BOOT_OK" in line:
  |             got = time.monotonic() - t0
  |             break
  |         if time.monotonic() - t0 > 60:
  |             break
  |     p.kill(); p.wait()
  |     print(f"{img.split("/")[-1]} {'seabios' if fw == 'seabios' else 'ovmf'} run{i+1}: "
  |           + (f"NOVA_BOOT_OK at {got:.2f} s" if got else "no NOVA_BOOT_OK within 60 s"))

